WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.850
Speaker 1: Welcome back to the David Pakman
show.

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:07.291
I'm Farron Cousins from a ring of fire sitting
in for David Pacman, but as I mentioned the

00:00:07.291 --> 00:00:13.380
beginning of the show, David will in fact
be back on Monday with fresh content for you.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.740
But for now, let's get right back to it.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:22.249
Of course, one of the biggest things this
week was the Turning Point USA Conference.

00:00:22.249 --> 00:00:27.050
And as we all know, one of the featured speakers
was Kyle Rittenhouse.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:33.980
And when Rittenhouse emerged onto that stage,
it was basically like WWE right there.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.780
He had his own theme song that they created
for him.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.739
So if you haven't already seen the video?

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:47.739
Brace yourselves, because here is Kyle Rittenhouse's
entrance into that Turning Point USA conference.

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:51.160
Take a look at loud.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.969
You know.

00:00:55.969 --> 00:01:39.170
The crowd loved him, you heard chanting Kyle
Kyle.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.930
But there was one person that was not happy
about this.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:49.150
There was one conservative who understood
that maybe this isn't the best guy to be hoisting

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.810
upon our collective shoulders.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:58.439
And believe it or not, folks, that person
happens to be Fox contributor Tomi Lahren.

00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:06.720
On an episode of Outnumbered this week, Lahren
actually can't say she laid into conservatives

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.200
for.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:14.290
Idolizing Kyle Rittenhouse, but she did question
why they're treating him like a rock star.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:17.220
Here is what she had to say.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:22.550
I do think that as conservatives, we need
to be a little careful when it comes to this.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:26.890
I believe we can put up Kyle Rittenhouse as
someone who was innocent and was bullied by

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.080
and mistreated by the media.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.480
But I think we should step back a little and
maybe not treat him like he's a rock star

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.090
or a celebrity.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:39.410
I don't think that's necessarily a good look
for the conservative movement.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.500
He did what he had to do.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.610
He was defending himself.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.620
Let's talk about self-defense.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:44.790
Let's talk about the riots.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:48.930
Let's talk about how everything went horribly,
horribly wrong that day.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:54.470
But I think we should take a step back and
not make the man Bon Jovi.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:56.440
But that's just my take.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.440
She says.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.480
Of course, that's how they're over.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.660
That's just my opinion.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:04.470
You know, don't don't kill the messenger.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.810
Here's the thing.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.330
She's right.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:17.690
It's a weird thing to say, but Tomi Lahren
is right, and she's right for several reasons.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.989
The first is.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:21.099
What's he done?

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:24.840
Well, let's be honest, we all know what happened.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.080
Two people are dead.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.700
Kyle Rittenhouse was acquitted.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.180
Now we could argue all day long whether or
not you think it was self-defense, whether

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.970
you think you should be here.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.620
But those arguments no longer really matter.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:38.620
OK?

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.970
Kyle Rittenhouse faced a jury.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:43.730
He had his defense.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:46.970
We had the prosecutors.

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:47.970
Defense prevailed.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.090
Kyle Rittenhouse was acquitted.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:53.360
That's the end of that, so we're not even
going to get into that.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.920
But two people are dead.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:59.010
And we know that he killed them, the court
says it's in self-defense, so we have to accept

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.489
that.

00:04:01.489 --> 00:04:03.230
And now he's a hero.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:04.319
Like now they're lifting him up.

00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:06.519
They gave him a speaking gig.

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:10.190
Now I'll be perfectly honest with you, I don't
know what he said.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.190
I didn't listen to it.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:12.900
I have no interest in listening to it.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.730
I don't care what he has to say.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:21.310
Although we do know that he did say in an
interview after the acquittal that, you know,

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.700
people shouldn't be praising him for this.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:27.040
I guess he's I guess he's OK with it now.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.500
But either way, Lauren's point, I think I
don't want to put words in your mouth, but

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.030
I think what she's trying to get at is why.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.290
What's the longevity?

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.190
Of Kyle Rittenhouse.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:44.980
What is he actually doing to further the conservative
cause?

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:49.880
So the answer to that question would obviously
be nothing.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:50.930
Not a thing.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:54.870
And, of course, Turning Point is supposed
to be about these conservatives who are out

00:04:54.870 --> 00:05:00.300
there making a difference, pushing their horrible
conservative policies on us, spitting out,

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.090
giving us new conservative talking points.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:06.990
But that's not what Kyle Rittenhouse is, he's
not a political operative.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:10.160
I mean, he's a kid.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.510
He's a kid that's now gotten swept up into
all of this.

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:17.110
And honestly, I don't think he understands
it either.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:20.470
I don't think he knows where he's going with
this.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:23.740
Does he have a future in the conservative
movement?

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.630
Does Kyle Rittenhouse have a shelf life?

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:30.220
And that's the big point that Tomi Lahren
herself is attempting to make.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.280
Think of it this way.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.880
I pointed this out actually on fair and balanced
as well.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:38.210
The McCloskeys right, the St. Louis gun couple.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:42.330
We all remember them, right?

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.600
What are they doing now?

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.060
They were conservative heroes.

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:52.550
Heck, they had a speaking spot at the GOP
convention last year, where are they now?

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.620
Are they still these conservative rising stars?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.530
I know I know the the guy was going to run
for Senate, and I don't think that went very

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.960
well for him.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:04.060
I don't even know if that's still happening
because nobody cares about the McCloskeys

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:05.750
anymore.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:09.550
And the same thing will eventually happen
to Kyle Rittenhouse.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:14.720
You know, maybe, you know, there's gun rights
organizations will try to use him as a poster

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.000
child.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.000
Maybe he'll do that.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.280
Maybe he won't.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.600
That's all pure speculation at this point,
to be honest.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:25.690
We don't know what he will or will not do
with this newfound fame.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:30.910
But one thing we can pretty much all come
to the same conclusion on is that based on

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.450
others who've been in this situation before,
the fame doesn't last.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:42.660
The spotlights fade, they disappear and people
will forget except the families affected who

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:47.380
this individual is and they won't care anymore.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:51.490
And I would like to think that that's what
Tomi Lahren was getting at.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:56.440
But I also think there could be a degree of
jealousy there, right?

00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:01.300
And let's face it, a couple of years ago,
Tomi Lahren was the it girl, right?

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.230
She was the one everybody was clamoring for.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:04.830
She was the one making the headlines.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:12.200
She was the one out there helping craft the
direction of the Republican Party.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:16.940
A lot of people forgot she existed.

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:22.930
So maybe, maybe and this is, you know, to
to pull a layer, that's just my opinion.

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:27.560
Maybe she's a little jealous of having to
share the spotlight.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:30.450
Maybe she's a little jealous that the spotlight
is not on her anymore.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.460
You know, people have moved on.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:38.120
And what's funny about that is I actually
said that many years ago when she first burst

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.330
onto the scene.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:44.570
Because I have been in this business for going
on 18 years.

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.660
We have seen them come and go.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:50.610
We have seen the fly by nighters, they make
a big pop, they make a big splash, they hang

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:54.240
around for a bit, sell a couple of books and
then they disappear.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:08:00.110
They fade off into obscurity because the Republican
movement, you know, this conservative media

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:04.690
thing, it's always trying to find the next
hero, trying to find the next big thing, trying

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:08.910
to find the next pretty face in many instances.

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:11.440
And Tommy Star is fading.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:18.090
Relegated to a weird show on Fox, having to
appear on a midday show to tell people that

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:22.250
it's a little cringeworthy what the Republicans
are doing with Kyle Rittenhouse.

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.560
Yeah.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:25.030
Next stop is Hollywood Squares.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:29.970
Maybe Dancing with the Stars and people will
have forgotten all about Tomi Lahren at that

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.210
point.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:34.870
And that's, I think, what really scares her
the most.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:40.370
Yes, conservatives should not be hoisting
Kyle Rittenhouse upon their shoulders.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.580
But Tomi Lahren speaks from experience.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:48.740
She knows what it's like as she knows how
much it hurts when you come crashing down

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:49.500
to reality

